NeoSCAD patch to manifold-rust 0.15.0 (crates.io): AddNewEdgeVerts, the
largest step of a boolean's result assembly, checks the cancel token at
each intersection and between the sorts after it, and allocates its lists
at their final size instead of growing them by doubling. Without a token
nothing changes, and with one that never fires the output is unchanged.
Tests: crates/geom/tests/kernel_cancel.rs and crates/web/test/run.mjs
(a measured memory limit on the gearbox example).

Upstream: proposed as branch `neoscad/cancel-new-edge-verts`
(commit 7620ada) of a fork of larsbrubaker/manifold-rust, on top of its
`main` at 40f20c6 (0.15.0 plus two QuickHull commits that touch none of
these files). This patch is that commit's changes under src/, byte for
byte apart from CRLF line endings; the branch also adds a benchmark
under examples/, which is not vendored.

Apply from the crate root on top of 0004: patch -p1 < this file.
The crate's older sources use CRLF line endings; files this series
adds use LF.
See vendor/README.md ("The cancellation patch").

